  "period_note": "Year-end position from ONE Bank Limited's FY2020 Annual Report, Solo basis. MAJOR FINDING: Total Shareholders' Equity reported here as 16,946.727m (Revaluation Reserve for Securities component: 11.908m); the FY2021 report's comparative balance sheet for 31.12.2020 instead shows Total Shareholders' Equity of 17,413.005m (Revaluation Reserve: 478.186m), with the entire +466.278m difference exactly offset by an equal decrease in Other Liabilities (28,862.725m to 28,396.447m) - i.e. a pure reclassification of part of a securities revaluation surplus out of 'Other Liabilities' into the equity-side 'Revaluation Reserve' line, with Total Assets and reported profit unaffected. Contemporaneous (16,946.727m) figure is retained per 'prefer contemporaneous'; both figures independently satisfy the balance-sheet identity. SECOND FINDING: Capital Surplus/(deficit) reported here as 1,030.704m (implying required capital = 24,919.851m, i.e. ~12.5% of this report's own RWA of 199,358.810m); the FY2021 report's comparative for FY2020 instead shows 6,014.674m (implying ~10.0% of the same RWA figure) - the RWA and Tier1/Tier2/Total Capital figures themselves are identical between the two reports, only the required-capital percentage embedded in the disclosed surplus changed. This is consistent with Bangladesh Bank's Capital Conservation Buffer having reached full phase-in (2.5%, i.e. 12.5% total) by FY2019/FY2020 before an apparent COVID-era relaxation back toward a 10% effective requirement reflected in later reports' comparatives - see sources.json. Contemporaneous 1,030.704m figure is retained. Provision surplus/(deficit) reported as nil ('-') in both this report and the FY2021 report's own comparative for FY2020 - see FY2021 note for the subsequent retroactive restatement of this specific figure starting with the FY2022 report.",
